---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PINNED_DATASET } from '../data/dataset-manifest';
import ProgressSummary from '../components/ProgressSummary.svelte';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Home"
  description="Free, no-account, no-server tools for opting out of data brokers and hardening your devices. Nothing leaves your browser -- verify it yourself."
>
  <h1>Make yourself expensive to track.</h1>

  <ProgressSummary client:load />

  <p>
    A free toolkit for making yourself a harder, more expensive target for surveillance and
    data-harvesting. The first section, <strong>Opt-Out</strong>, walks you through getting your
    data out of the data-broker economy by hand, without handing it to a paid service to do it
    for you. Guides for hardening your own devices are next.
  </p>

  <h2>Why this is different</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No server touches your information.</strong> This is a static page. Your name,
      address, and progress are stored only in this browser, never sent anywhere.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>You don't have to take our word for it.</strong> The code is open source — read it
      yourself, or have someone technical you trust read it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No account, no signup.</strong> Nothing to create, nothing to lose access to.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The broker data is a public commons</strong>, not something this app owns —
      it credits and builds on prior public research, and this app is just one way to use it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="build-info">
    Dataset version <code>{PINNED_DATASET.datasetVersion}</code>, content hash
    <code>{PINNED_DATASET.contentHash.slice(0, 16)}…</code> — verified against this build on load.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting started</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Start with a handful, not the whole list.</strong> There are hundreds of brokers,
    and working through them in order of what actually matters — a few per sitting — is the
    difference between finishing and bouncing off. That's what the guided flow does: it picks
    the next batch for you, easiest and highest-value first.
  </p>
  <p>
    Setting up a profile first is optional. It stays on this device and only pre-fills the
    opt-out emails and forms you send yourself, plus picks the right legal citation for your
    state. You can skip it, though rows that compose an email or have fields to copy will be
    blank until you fill it in.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/brokers/guide/">Start opting out →</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp;
    <a href="/profile">Set up your profile first →</a>
  </p>
  <p class="secondary-link">
    Looking for a specific broker? <a href="/brokers">Browse the full list →</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .secondary-link {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--graphite);
  }
  .build-info {
    font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--graphite);
  }
</style>
